  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Enhancing the Efficiency and Effectiveness of Humanitarian Logistics through a Common Pipeline Management Database Application, Global Action</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In line with the Humanitarian Implementation Plan (HIP) for Enhanced Response Capacity (ERC), IOM is improving global humanitarian supply chain operations through the development and roll-out of a new version of IOM&apos;s innovative Common Pipeline Management online database application. Common Pipelines allow for the joint procurement, transport, pre-positioning, and storage of relief items by one agency on behalf of pipeline partners. Through this proposed project, IOM intends to support Shelter and Water, Sanitation and Hygiene clusters by providing available and accessible supply chain data, to allow the clusters to take faster, more comprehensive decisions, thus ensuring faster and more efficient responses.This application will be available to organizations leading Common Pipeline operations, and will be available to be used by all pipeline partners for making stock requests. Throughout this project, IOM is leveraging its expertise in supply chain management and 10+ years of experience in managing Common Pipeline operations.</narrative>
  </description>
